# Intent: The offline mumble, device side (owner decision 24; core UX16, spec docs/design/offline-mumble.md). A caption sentence the host sends with "mumble": true (it has no voice for it) is mumbled when the setting mumble is on (default off), captions are on and the sound policy allows: one code-made note per character timed to the caption, rendered 200 ms at a time into the audio queue at the chime level, with the face's mouth following the note that sounds. Mute, sounds off and quiet hours silence the sound only; the mouth still moves. It ends at once on the wake word, the stop word or an abort, and a new sentence replaces it. The unit announces the feature in its hello (features.mumble) so the host sends the flag only to units that have it.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_mumble.cc, maipai_mumble_render_core.h (ours); small hooks in application.cc, websocket_protocol.cc, maipai_facefx.cc, maipai_tbprefs
# Check after a flash: set the pref mumble to true, turn captions on, send a tts sentence_start with text and "mumble": true while no audio plays: notes sound in step with the words, the mouth moves with them and closes at the end, the log shows "MAIPAI-MUMBLE: start" then "end"; with mute on the mouth moves and nothing sounds; the wake word ends it; with the pref off nothing happens. Read the mouth against the sound to set kLatencyMs (120 ms is an estimate). Plain boot memory gate unchanged.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_OFFLINE_MUMBLE (default y)
# Memory cost: while it plays: a 12.8 KB buffer and at most 401 bytes of text in PSRAM, freed when it ends; internal RAM about 250 bytes of state while idle (one mm_t, a 12-note ring, a mutex, an esp_timer created on first use); flash about 3 KB (estimate). Nothing is held while no mumble plays.

